                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 3 at 2:24PM EDT until October 5 at 8:00AM EDT by NWS Tallahassee FL",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of Big Bend and Panhandle Florida, including the\nfollowing areas, in Big Bend Florida, Coastal Bay. In Panhandle\nFlorida, Central Walton, Coastal Gulf, Holmes, Inland Bay, Inland\nGulf, North Walton, South Walton and Washington.\n\n* WHEN...Through Monday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional rainfall totals (beginning tonight through Monday) of\n3 to 7 inches are forecast with the lower end of these ranges\nmore likely across out SW Georgia and Florida Big Bend counties\nand the higher end of these totals more likely across the\nPanhandle and into extreme southern portions of Alabama. Locally\nhigher amounts of 7 to 10 inches are possible along the Emerald\nCoast by the time we get to early Monday morning.\n\n- Http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
